<p>For a stage-by-stage walkthrough of what happens when, see our <a href="/blogs/interior-design-timeline/">interior design timeline guide</a>.</p>
<h3>Payment structure that protects you</h3>
<p>A fair, milestone-linked schedule looks like: <strong>10% booking → 40% on material/factory order → 40% on delivery and installation milestones → 10% on snag-free handover</strong>. Walk away from anyone demanding 70–80% before work begins, and hold that final 10% until every snag on your punch list is closed.</p>
<h4>How we compiled these figures</h4>
<p>Cost ranges reflect quoted and executed renovation projects in the Bangalore and Hosur market as of Q2–Q3 2026, at prevailing material, labour, and civil-work rates. Ranges are intentionally wide because renovation cost depends heavily on property age and condition — factors invisible until demolition.</p>
<p>This article is general guidance, not a quotation. For numbers specific to your home's age, layout, and condition, request an itemised estimate after a site visit — no renovation quote given without seeing the property should be trusted as final.</p>
